STATS_HELP = """cc4a stats — token totals for Claude sessions on this host.

USAGE
  cc4a stats [--since=<dur>] [--by=<dim>] [--top=N] [--json]

  --since=  window, as <n>s / <n>m / <n>h / <n>d. Default 5h, the rate-limit window.
  --by=     session (default), project, model, or day
  --top=    rows to show, default 10. --json always returns every row.

WHAT THE NUMBERS MEAN
  Four token counts are recorded per assistant message, and only three of them
  are additive across a session:

    output        tokens generated. The truest measure of work done.
    cache-write   context written to cache. Real, paid once.
    input         uncached input. Usually tiny.
    cache-read    cached prefix re-counted on EVERY turn of the session.

  cache-read dominates any naive total — commonly 90-95% of it — because a long
  session re-reads the same prefix hundreds of times. Summing all four produces a
  number that mostly measures session length, not consumption. This tool ranks by
  output and reports the components separately. Treat any tool quoting one big
  "tokens used" figure with suspicion.

  Percentages are shares of the window's total, NOT of a rate limit. Anthropic
  publishes no token denominator for the 5h or 7d windows (see `cc4a usage`), so a
  session's share of your quota is not a computable number. Do not present it as one.

  Session ids are truncated for display; --json carries them in full.
"""

